    "evidence_framing": {
      "bypass_note": "The 5.8 mb/d East-West figure (Saudi energy minister, 6 Oct 2026; original wording archived in research/logs/2026-10-06.md) is treated as a reported operating rate as of that date, with an unverified sustained average. Context for why a partial-recovery comparison is worth showing \u2014 not an input to any number in this output.",
      "momentum_note": "September's rebound does not establish uninterrupted momentum (EIA Table 3c: Saudi Jul 2026 9.35 mb/d > Sep 2026 9.29 mb/d), and the four-country table excludes the UAE, Bahrain, Qatar and Oman.",
      "flat_judgment_note": "The published v2 standoff's flat level is the judgment 'the recovery stops at the reported September level'. This line measures how much that judgment matters by Dec 2027: it is exactly half the gap between the issued path and the EIA baseline's own balance from the same starting point."
    }
